Description: Fix parent/sizer mismatch in the progress dialog (gaugePanel)
 gaugePanel builds an inner wx.Panel to hold the label and gauge, but
 never calls panel.SetSizer() on it; instead the inner sizer itself is
 added directly to the dialog's outer sizer. The label and gauge
 widgets are therefore managed by a sizer nested under the dialog's
 sizer while their real parent (the inner panel) is never part of that
 hierarchy at all.
 .
 wxWidgets 3.2 (as currently shipped by Debian/Ubuntu) enforces this at
 runtime and aborts with a C++ assertion; older wxWidgets versions
 tolerated it. gaugePanel is mMassX's shared progress dialog, used for
 every long-running operation (opening a file, exporting, processing),
 so this crashed on the very first file open:
 .
   wx._core.wxAssertionError: C++ assertion
   "CheckExpectedParentIs(w, m_containingWindow)" failed at
   ./src/common/sizer.cpp(887) in SetContainingWindow(): Windows
   managed by the sizer associated with the given window must have
   this window as parent, otherwise they will not be repositioned
   correctly.
 .
 Fix: give the inner panel its own sizer, and add the panel itself
 (not its sizer) to the outer sizer.
Author: David <david@katalystnord.com>
Forwarded: https://github.com/SCIENCE-OPEN/mmassx/pull/2
Last-Update: 2026-09-08
--- a/gui/mwx.py
+++ b/gui/mwx.py
@@ -714,10 +714,11 @@ class gaugePanel(wx.Dialog):
         sizer = wx.BoxSizer(wx.VERTICAL)
         sizer.Add(self.label, 0, wx.BOTTOM, 5)
         sizer.Add(self.gauge, 0, wx.EXPAND, 0)
-        
+        panel.SetSizer(sizer)
+
         mainSizer = wx.BoxSizer(wx.VERTICAL)
-        mainSizer.Add(sizer, 0, wx.ALL, PANEL_SPACE_MAIN)
-        
+        mainSizer.Add(panel, 0, wx.ALL, PANEL_SPACE_MAIN)
+
         self.Layout()
         mainSizer.Fit(self)
         self.SetSizer(mainSizer)
